      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not intended, thanks. In patch set 5 only HTTP/2 passes the reader a limit, so readers under a Beast parser, including http_client\u0027s, rely on its body_limit again. A new test parses a chunked response one byte over the limit as http_client does. It passes on patch set 5 and fails with patch set 4\u0027s always-on reader limit forced back in. Separately, reader::init() on master already rejects a declared Content-Length over 1024 * 1024 * BMCWEB_HTTP_BODY_LIMIT; I can fix that in a follow-up.",
